@startuml
/' docs/sds/diagrams/plugin-install.puml — package to enabled plugin, then containment at runtime.
   Implements: SDS §8. Register: C-8 (fourth service), C-9 (no publisher CA, D27),
   C-13 (migration grammar), O-36 (asset guard per plugin table), O-37 (test report),
   O-44 (write-only secrets). '/
title Plugin install, enable, and the RPC containment boundary

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam maxMessageSize 130

actor "Tenant owner" as O
participant "app  admin" as APP
participant "plugin-runner" as RUN
participant "site.db" as DB
participant "data/trust/" as TR

== Install: signature, then review, then DDL ==

O -> APP : upload plugin-<id>-<version>.tar.gz
APP -> APP : verify package root signature\nfirst-party: the key baked into the image\nthird-party: a key the OWNER imported
APP -> TR : read publishers.json (per-install, written only by the owner)\nread revoked.json (local to the install)
alt signature unknown or root revoked
  APP --> O : 409 SKW_E_PL_SIGNATURE / SKW_E_PL_REVOKED
end
note right of APP
  There is **no publisher CA** (C-9 / D27).
  Our key verifies first-party packages only;
  no key we hold signs, countersigns or revokes
  a third party. The fingerprint is shown
  beside every capability on this screen.
end note

APP -> APP : validate plugin.json\nid ^[a-z][a-z0-9]{1,19}$ · cms range · tables[] · settings[]\nadmin forms · public endpoints · capabilities
APP -> APP : require test-report.json whose runner_image_digest\nmatches this image
alt report missing or stale
  APP --> O : 409 SKW_E_PL_TESTS_STALE
end

APP -> RUN : run the plugin's own tests against a scratch site.db\n(same image, same containment)
RUN --> APP : test-report.json

APP -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE
APP -> DB : apply forward-only migrations through the HOST executor\nops subset: create_table · add_column · create_index · drop_index\n  NO drop_table, NO rename, NO drop_column (grammar, not policy)
APP -> DB : CREATE TABLE p_<id>_*  (prefix CHECK GLOB 'p_?*')\n+ trg_asset_guard_p_<id>_<table> for every asset_key column\n+ row in cms_trigger_registry (purpose='asset_delete_guard')
APP -> DB : row in cms_plugin_migration(plugin_id, version, seq)\nrow in cms_table_registry(table_class='plugin')
APP -> DB : row in cms_plugin_installed(enabled=0, manifest_json, root_hash)
APP -> DB : postcondition: every table is cms_* | u_* | p_* | sqlite_* -> else ABORT
APP -> DB : COMMIT
note right of DB
  A p_* table's export class comes from
  manifest_json.tables[].export. No class ->
  install refused, SKW_E_PL_NO_EXPORT_CLASS,
  because a table nobody classified cannot be
  sold (C-5).
end note

== Enable ==

O -> APP : enable  (capabilities listed, fingerprints shown)
APP -> APP : secrets are write-only: settings.get -> null,\nsettings.has -> boolean, admin shows ••••••
APP -> DB : UPDATE cms_plugin_installed SET enabled=1, enabled_at=?
APP -> RUN : spawn one node --permission child for this package
note right of RUN
  --allow-fs-read limited to the package and its scratch dir.
  No --allow-addons, no --allow-child-process, no --allow-worker.
  Container: network_mode: none, read_only: true,
  cap_drop: [ALL], pids_limit: 64.
  With addons on, ATTACH to a sibling tenant succeeds —
  measured. With them off, new Database() fails
  ERR_DLOPEN_DISABLED.
end note

== Runtime: 14 operations, no fifth door ==

O -> APP : a page posts to the plugin's public endpoint
APP -> RUN : store.insert(table,row)   row<=32KiB, <=24 declared columns
RUN --> APP : ok
APP -> DB : the HOST writes the row (the plugin never holds a handle)
APP --> O : 200

note over APP, RUN
  **Operations that exist (14):**
  store.insert · store.update · store.delete · store.query · store.count
  settings.get · settings.has · settings.set · assets.resolve · mail.send
  log.write · util.now · util.random · util.hash
end note
note over APP, RUN
  **Absent by decision, each absence a control:**
  sql · exec · prepare · db · attach · fs.* · net.* · http.* · fetch · env
  require/import outside the package · worker · spawn
  assets.write · assets.upload · mail.raw · tenant.* · cms.*
  store.raw · store.join · cron · stream
end note

alt plugin hangs or dies
  APP -> RUN : 2 s per-op timeout, circuit breaker opens
  APP --> O : 503 SKW_E_PL_UNAVAILABLE on that endpoint only
  note right of APP
    No plugin code is on the render path, so a
    broken plugin degrades one endpoint. It
    cannot take a page down (P-1).
  end note
end

@enduml
